Team,

The chilled store at Kharar is twelve years old and its panels have moved, so we are surveying the outside of the envelope every quarter from now on.

The survey is done with the borrowed infrared camera, at night, after the store has held its set point for at least a day. We look at panel joints, door frames, cable entries and the line where the walls meet the floor.

Any joint that shows more than 2 C colder than the panel face next to it is marked with chalk, resealed by the panel contractor within a week and surveyed again. The old store's foam is thin, so we are stricter here than we would be in a new building.

Save the images with the wall reference and the date, and print the marked ones for the maintenance file. The quarterly thermography report goes to me by e-mail.

If you find ice on the outside of a panel, do not wait for the survey; report it the same day.

Please do not survey on a sunny afternoon or after rain; warm or wet walls hide the cold spots and we end up resealing the wrong joints. Two people go on every survey, one with the camera and one with the chalk and the clipboard, and both sign the sheet.

Rajinder
